WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:00.973
Hello, I'm Gav.

00:00:00.973 --> 00:00:01.806
I'm Dan.

00:00:01.806 --> 00:00:02.639
We're the Slow Mo Guys.

00:00:02.639 --> 00:00:04.690
I've always been interested in how

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.210
fire spreads against a sort of

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.860
solid, horizontal surface.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:09.693
Yeah.

00:00:09.693 --> 00:00:11.040
And like, you know, if you like throw

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.830
a bucket of petrol at a wall or something.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:13.890
Yeah.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.723
I always thought it'd be cool to look

00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.040
at fire from the other side of that.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.430
What, like, so as if it
was like see-through?

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.263
Yeah.

00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:21.220
Like glass?

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.183
Something like glass, yeah.

00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:23.193
Like this glass?

00:00:24.353 --> 00:00:25.186
Yeah.

00:00:26.055 --> 00:00:27.330
Not the first time we've
done that joke, is it?

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:28.163
No.

00:00:29.072 --> 00:00:31.400
So, if you throw a
bucket of petrol on fire

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.350
sort of right here, hopefully in lovely,

00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.910
glorious 4K slow mo, we'll see the fire

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.960
spread all throughout
and you'll be able to see

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:41.210
it against like a flat,
perfectly in focused surface.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.350
Oh, yeah, that's a good point.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:43.450
It's going to be perfectly in focus

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:44.360
'cause it's a level plane.

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.772
It's going to be like a cross
section of fire, isn't it?

00:00:46.772 --> 00:00:47.605
Yeah.

00:00:47.605 --> 00:00:48.438
It should be lovely.

00:00:48.438 --> 00:00:49.280
And incredibly dangerous.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.927
Please don't do this at home.

00:00:50.927 --> 00:00:52.770
As you can see, we're
not at anyone's home,

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:53.603
we're in a quarry.

00:00:53.603 --> 00:00:54.436
Yeah.

00:00:54.436 --> 00:00:55.830
We've done this in someone else's quarry.

00:00:55.830 --> 00:00:56.663
Yeah.

00:00:57.574 --> 00:00:59.680
Okay, dangerous experiment so

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.160
precautionary measures are in order.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.590
Getting the danger suit on.

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:04.890
So it's like flame retardant overalls,

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:08.670
flame retardant balaclava, goggles,

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.453
flame retardant gloves.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.350
All for just a little bit of petrol.

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:16.900
Is it enjoyable wearing this

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:19.810
on a 37 degree day in Texas?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:20.643
Hell, no.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.143
Eyes here.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:25.330
I'm gonna be positioned

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:26.410
there with the camera

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:28.520
zoomed in enough to fill the frame.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:29.880
That's about as far away as I can be,

00:01:29.880 --> 00:01:31.140
because it's gonna be night email

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:33.550
and then we've both
got fire extinguishers.

00:01:33.550 --> 00:01:35.200
You're gonna use yours on the window.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:36.730
I'm gonna use mine on the window.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:38.810
Well, not necessarily the window,

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.370
but all of the other stuff

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.203
in case we need to-
Like the

00:01:41.203 --> 00:01:42.036
flammable cardboard.

00:01:42.036 --> 00:01:42.869
Pretty much.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:43.702
In case you need to do another shot,

00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:44.535
so I'm gonna get straight in there

00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:45.368
with the fire extinguisher

00:01:45.368 --> 00:01:47.180
and put it right out, to
stop any sort of flames.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:48.200
And my fire extinguisher's

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.280
gonna be for you.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.450
I'm gonna drag that right
close to the camera.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.730
And I'll run in and put you out,

00:01:52.730 --> 00:01:54.240
just in case it all goes wrong.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:55.670
If I haven't put myself out already.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:56.503
Yeah.

00:01:57.387 --> 00:01:58.380
Yeah, I need to pee as well,

00:01:58.380 --> 00:01:59.460
so we've also got that.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.610
So, order of runnings.

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.520
You're gonna light it,

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.353
you're gonna throw it.

00:02:03.353 --> 00:02:04.670
I'm gonna bag the camera.

00:02:04.670 --> 00:02:05.560
Yeah.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.600
Then you extinguish the cardboard

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:09.500
and if you're on fire,

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.900
I run in and extinguish you.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:12.303
Before anything else.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:15.070
Oh, I was gonna have lunch first.

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.442
You ready?

00:02:16.442 --> 00:02:17.730
Ready.

00:02:17.730 --> 00:02:19.470
Just gonna dump my hands in this water.

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:20.303
Okay.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.870
Okay, I'm ready.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:24.934
Okay.

00:02:24.934 --> 00:02:25.767
I'm gonna go ahead.

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:27.434
All right.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.073
Here we go.

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.013
You good?

00:02:39.013 --> 00:02:39.846
Yeah, we're good.

00:02:39.846 --> 00:02:40.679
Get the camera.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.680
Good?

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:49.252
Go for it.

00:02:52.695 --> 00:02:53.795
Part of it, the glass.

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:57.973
Nice.

00:03:00.140 --> 00:03:00.973
Excellent.

00:03:02.563 --> 00:03:03.620
There was no splash back on me.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:04.453
That's good.

00:03:04.453 --> 00:03:05.640
But I would've liked to have thrown

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.250
